# Front-end F1 part B: byte-pinned build inputs. These files are compiled into the binary
# (`include_str!`/`include!` in crates/lottery/src/embedded.rs) or compared line by line
# (crates/lottery/tests/f1_bytes.rs), and are committed with LF endings. `-text` turns off
# every end-of-line conversion for them (core.autocrlf included), so a Windows checkout
# holds the committed bytes exactly.
crates/lottery/templates/** -text
crates/lottery/tests/fixtures/f1_digests.txt -text
# F1 part C: the API digests (crates/web/tests/api.rs and w1_wasm.rs compare against them).
crates/web/tests/fixtures/w1_api.txt -text
# F1 review: the verify-call digests (crates/web/tests/api.rs and w1_wasm.rs compare against them).
crates/web/tests/fixtures/w1_verify.txt -text
# Front end F6 part B: the framed figures. Their inline script and style elements are pinned by hash in
# web/vercel.json (the figure CSP), so the committed bytes must reach every checkout and Vercel unchanged.
web/public/figures/*.html -text
